To run the pytest, use:
pytest [options]

Options:
-v - verbose
-x - stop on first fail
-s - transfer console output to pytest output
-k key_word - runs only files and tests with key_word in the name in the current directory and subdirectories
file_name - specify file name to run all tests in the file
-m 'mark_names expression' - to run cases with specified mark names. supports "not mark_name" and combinations

Pytest file should start with 'test_' or end with '_test'
Tests should start with 'test' key word

Annotations:
@pytest.mark.[mark_name] - marks should be registered in pytest.ini file
Pytest built in marks:
skip - to skip the test from the execution
skipif - conditional tests skipping
xfail - test where fail is expected. Used to mark the test suit as passed
parametrize("par1, par2", [(v1, s1), (v2, s2)] - to run the same test against a set of parameters

Fixtures:
Fixture is a function that contains steps that are executed before and after the actual test case.
e.g. Setup and teardown needed for the test:
- establish and close connection
- envoke the browser and clear out cookie files
To define a fixture add @pytest.fixture() before function definition
To add fixture to a test, add the name of the fixture to the test definition def test_name(fixture_name)
Steps before yeild keyword are executed before the test, steps after yeild are executed after
Fixtures defined in the test file are available for the tests in the file.
Fixtures defined in conftest.py file are available to all tests in the directory and sub-directories.
Several conftest files can be defined at different levels of the hierarchyof the project.
Several fixtures could be added to the test def test_name(global_setup_teardown, local_setup_teardown)
Each fixture will be executed in a specified sequence
Fixture name shadowing (scope):

Each conftest file makes all fixtures
If the same fixture name is used in local files and several conftest files.
Pytest follows upward rule in fixture definition:
- local file
- closest to test file conftest.py
...
- furthest to test file conftest.py